'' --diagnostics-file naming a path that cannot be written is a command-line error, at the
'' start, not a silent loss at the end: DiagOut.Start creates the file before anything is
'' compiled.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --diagnostics-file build/.diagfile-no-such-dir/x.tsv --parse-only tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0117: cannot write the diagnostics file 'build/.diagfile-no-such-dir/x.tsv'
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.diagfile-no-such-dir/x.tsv
